<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">1977</h1><p class="ref-lede">1977 in world history: 11 events, 2 births, 21 deaths, 1 state founded and 1 that came to an end. 204 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/1973">1973</a><a href="/years/1974">1974</a><a href="/years/1975">1975</a><a href="/years/1976">1976</a><a href="/years/1977" aria-current="page">1977</a><a href="/years/1978">1978</a><a href="/years/1979">1979</a><a href="/years/1980">1980</a><a href="/years/1981">1981</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-27">27 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Two jumbo jets collide at Tenerife</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A KLM 747 began its take-off in fog and struck a Pan Am 747 on the runway at Los Rodeos airport, killing 583 people. It remains the deadliest accident in aviation history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-25">25 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Star Wars opens in American cinemas</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">George Lucas's space adventure opened in a few dozen cinemas and became the highest-grossing film to that date. It reshaped Hollywood around the blockbuster and merchandising.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-16">16 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Elvis Presley dies at Graceland</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">Elvis Presley was found dead at his Memphis home, aged 42. The 'King of Rock and Roll' had sold hundreds of millions of records and transformed popular music.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-19">19 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Anwar Sadat becomes the first Arab leader to visit Israel</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s president <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anwar-sadat">Anwar Sadat</a> flew to Israel and the next day addressed the Knesset in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>. His visit led to the Camp <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a> Accords and the 1979 Egyptian-Israeli peace treaty.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/torrijos-carter-treaties" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/torrijos-carter-treaties.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/torrijos-carter-treaties">Torrijos–Carter Treaties</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Torrijos–Carter Treaties were two agreements signed on 7 September 1977 by Panama's leader Omar Torrijos and US President Jimmy Carter.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Treaty</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal-neutrality-treaty">Treaty Concerning the Permanent Neutrality and Operation of the Panama Canal</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty Concerning the Permanent Neutrality and Operation of the Panama Canal, usually called the Neutrality Treaty, was one of the two Torrijos–Carter Treaties signed by Panama and the United States in 1977.</p></div></li></ol></section>
